From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: programs pinned to the taskbar

David: "you can pin one of the open icons to the panel and it remains
there". The pins are shortcuts where Windows keeps them --
%APPDATA%\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Quick Launch\User Pinned\TaskBar,
where installers and programs that pin themselves write too -- in the order
HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Taskbar PinOrder (REG_MULTI_SZ of their file
names) lists; others follow by name. New file taskpins.c keeps them.

- A running program's button menu offers "Pin to taskbar" / "Unpin from
  taskbar"; pinning writes a shortcut named after the program and puts it
  last in the order.
- A pinned program that is not running has an icon button of its own,
  first after Start and search: a click starts it, its menu starts or
  unpins it. Running, its windows' buttons stand in the pin's place.
- The bar reads the pins again on "TraySettings", so Start and Settings
  can pin and reorder.

Gate: test/taskpins-gate.sh (pin, close, start from the pin, unpin).
